\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Raise the psalm : let earth adoring,
\par Through each kindred, tribe, and tongue,
\par To her God His praise restoring,
\par Raise the new accordant song.
\par Bless His name, each farthest nation;
\par Sing His praise, His truth display :
\par Tell anew His high salvation
\par With each new return of day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Tell it out beneath the heaven,
\par To each kindred, tribe, and tongue,
\par Tell it out from morn till even
\par In your unexhausted song :
\par Tell that God for ever reigneth,
\par He, who set the world so fast,
\par He, who still its state sustaineth 
\par Till the day of doom to last.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Tell them that the day is coming 
\par When that righteous doom shall be;
\par Then shall heaven new joys illumine,
\par Gladness shine o'ver earth and sea.
\par Yea, the far-resounding ocean
\par Shall its thousand voices raise, 
\par All its waves in glad commotion 
\par Chant the fullness of His praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And earth's fields, with herbs and flowers,
\par Shall put on their choice array,
\par And in all their leafy bowers 
\par Shall the woods keep holy-day :
\par When the judge, to earth descending,
\par Righteous judgement shall ordain,
\par Fraud and wrong shall then have ending,
\par Truth, immortal truth, shall reign.  
\par                                       Amen.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

